> However, there _is_ a known issue right now with the level compiler
> that might cause something to be misaligned; it has to do with the order
> things are put onto the map, which is different between Spork and
> vanilla.  Once we fix that bug, this sort of thing will likely go away
> (except of course for bones).

Explanation: This is a bug where a room is generated with it's contents
and then a subroom is generated "on top of" or "inside" that room.
The outer room doesn't know there will be a subroom inside it, so
some of the contents, such as monsters, may get generated inside the
inner room, possibly even in the walls of the inner room.

What probably happened here is that a monster was generated in the
outer room exactly on the place where the Oracle would be in the
inner room.  When the inner room was generated and Oracle was
places in there, the outer room monster already occupied
that position.  Therefore Oracle was displaced.

